  "problem": "Let $f(t)$ be a piecewise continuous function on $[0,\\infty )$ with exponential order $a,$ and consider its Laplace transform\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)},\\,s>a.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $f(t)$ is of exponential order $a,$ then the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,dt$ converges for every $s>a.$\n- If $f(t)$ is of exponential order $a,$ then its Laplace transform $F(s)$ exists for all $s>a.$\n- The Laplace transform of any piecewise continuous function of exponential order is infinitely differentiable in its region of convergence.",
